IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgn-notices`

-- Tests for sgn-notices.l4 (ss 386AG, 386AH, 386AI, 386AIA, 386AJ, 386AK). Expected values are written from the text beside each assertion.
-- A prescribed period is a number of days; the tests use 14 days (assumed, not text), counted from 1 June 2026, so the last day is 15 June 2026.

`s 386AG test company` MEANS Company "Acme Pte Ltd"
`s 386AG test addressee` MEANS Individual "B"
`s 386AK test person` MEANS Individual "P"

§ `s 386AG(1): reasonable steps`

#ASSERT `s 386AG(1) the company or foreign company has complied with the duty to take reasonable steps` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no time is fixed and no offence follows (1), so not yet done is not a failure the text names
#ASSERT `s 386AG(1) the company or foreign company has complied with the duty to take reasonable steps` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the duty has no time limit: it can be fulfilled, or stay open, but no trace can show it breached (listed under "Rules with no breach path")
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AG(1) a company or foreign company must take reasonable steps to find out and identify its registrable controllers` `s 386AG test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AG test company` DOES `s 386AG(1) take reasonable steps to find out and identify the registrable controllers` AT 3
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 386AG(1) a company or foreign company must take reasonable steps to find out and identify its registrable controllers` `s 386AG test company` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `s 386AG(2) and (4): whom the company must give a notice to`

-- arguments: knows the person is a registrable controller; knows the person knows who one is; all the information was previously provided
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the company or foreign company must give a notice to the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the company or foreign company must give a notice to the person` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the company or foreign company must give a notice to the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a person in neither class: the subsection does not speak
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the company or foreign company must give a notice to the person` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- subsection (4): all the information was previously provided, so no notice is required of the person
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the company or foreign company must give a notice to the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the company or foreign company must give a notice to the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the company or foreign company must give a notice to the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 386AG(2): what the notice must require`

-- arguments: the paragraph; requires (a)(i) the statement whether a controller; requires (a)(ii) and (b)(i) the statement about another person; requires (a)(iii) and (b)(ii) the other information
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the notice requires what the paragraph requires` `s 386AG(2)(a) a notice to a person the company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, is a registrable controller` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the notice requires what the paragraph requires` `s 386AG(2)(a) a notice to a person the company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, is a registrable controller` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the notice requires what the paragraph requires` `s 386AG(2)(a) a notice to a person the company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, is a registrable controller` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the notice requires what the paragraph requires` `s 386AG(2)(a) a notice to a person the company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, is a registrable controller` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- paragraph (b) lists only two items, so the first does not matter
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the notice requires what the paragraph requires` `s 386AG(2)(b) a notice to a person the company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, knows the identity of a registrable controller or is likely to have that knowledge` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the notice requires what the paragraph requires` `s 386AG(2)(b) a notice to a person the company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, knows the identity of a registrable controller or is likely to have that knowledge` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(2) the notice requires what the paragraph requires` `s 386AG(2)(b) a notice to a person the company knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, knows the identity of a registrable controller or is likely to have that knowledge` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 386AG(3): the notice's content and the time to give it`

-- arguments: states the time for compliance; is in the prescribed form, with the prescribed particulars, sent in the prescribed manner
#ASSERT `s 386AG(3)(a) and (b) the notice is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(3)(a) and (b) the notice is as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(3)(a) and (b) the notice is as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(3)(a) and (b) the notice is as the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- arguments: given; the day given; the day the company first knew; the prescribed period in days; the date asked
#ASSERT `s 386AG(3)(c) the company or foreign company has given the notice in time` TRUE (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(3)(c) the company or foreign company has given the notice in time` TRUE (Date 16 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(3)(c) the company or foreign company has given the notice in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 (Date 16 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(3)(c) the company or foreign company has given the notice in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AG(2) and (3)(c) a company or foreign company must give the notice within the prescribed period after it first knows` `s 386AG test company` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AG test company` DOES `s 386AG(2) give a notice to the person` AT 14
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AG(2) and (3)(c) a company or foreign company must give the notice within the prescribed period after it first knows` `s 386AG test company` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AG test company` DOES `s 386AG(2) give a notice to the person` AT 15

§ `s 386AG(5): the offence of the company and the officers in default`

#ASSERT `s 386AG(5) the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(5) the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- arguments: fails to comply; the person is an officer in default (s 408(3))
#ASSERT `s 386AG(5) the officer of the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(5) the officer of the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(5) the officer of the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- arguments: fails to comply; the person is the company; the person is an officer in default. A fine not exceeding $25,000.
#ASSERT `s 386AG(5) the most the company or foreign company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 386AG(5) the most the company or foreign company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 386AG(5) the most the company or foreign company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 386AG(5) the most the company or foreign company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 386AG(6) and (7): the addressee`

-- arguments: the person is the addressee of a notice under (2); the information is subject to legal privilege
#ASSERT `s 386AG(6) the addressee is required to provide the information` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(6) the addressee is required to provide the information` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(6) the addressee is required to provide the information` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 386AG(6) the addressee is required to provide the information` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- arguments: complied; the day complied; the date specified in the notice; the date asked
#ASSERT `s 386AG(6) the addressee has complied with the notice within the time specified` TRUE (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(6) the addressee has complied with the notice within the time specified` TRUE (Date 11 6 2026) (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(6) the addressee has complied with the notice within the time specified` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 11 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(6) the addressee has complied with the notice within the time specified` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 10 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AG(6) an addressee must comply with the notice within the time specified in it` `s 386AG test addressee` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AG test addressee` DOES `s 386AG(6) comply with the notice` AT 7
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AG(6) an addressee must comply with the notice within the time specified in it` `s 386AG test addressee` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AG test addressee` DOES `s 386AG(6) comply with the notice` AT 8
#ASSERT `s 386AG(7) the addressee is guilty of the offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(7) the addressee is guilty of the offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AG(7) the most the addressee may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 386AG(7) the most the addressee may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 386AH: keeping information up to date`

-- (7): arguments: a person ceases to be a registrable controller; any other change makes the particulars incorrect or incomplete
#ASSERT `s 386AH(7) a relevant change occurs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(7) a relevant change occurs` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(7) a relevant change occurs` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) and (4): arguments: knows or has reasonable grounds to believe a relevant change has occurred; all the information was previously provided
#ASSERT `s 386AH(1) the company or foreign company must give notice to the registrable controller` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(1) the company or foreign company must give notice to the registrable controller` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(1) the company or foreign company must give notice to the registrable controller` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(1) the company or foreign company must give notice to the registrable controller` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) content: arguments: confirm whether or not the change occurred; if it occurred, the date; if it occurred, the particulars
#ASSERT `s 386AH(1) the notice requires what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(1) the notice requires what the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(1) the notice requires what the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(1) the notice requires what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): arguments: given; the day given; the day first knew; the prescribed period in days; the date asked
#ASSERT `s 386AH(2) the company or foreign company has given the notice in time` TRUE (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(2) the company or foreign company has given the notice in time` TRUE (Date 16 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(2) the company or foreign company has given the notice in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 (Date 16 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(2) the company or foreign company has given the notice in time` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2026) 14 (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AH(1) and (2) a company or foreign company must give the notice within the prescribed period after it first knows of the change` `s 386AG test company` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AG test company` DOES `s 386AH(1) give notice to the registrable controller` AT 14
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AH(1) and (2) a company or foreign company must give the notice within the prescribed period after it first knows of the change` `s 386AG test company` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AG test company` DOES `s 386AH(1) give notice to the registrable controller` AT 15
-- (3): arguments: states the time for compliance; is in the prescribed form and manner
#ASSERT `s 386AH(3) the notice is as section 386AG(3)(a) and (b) require` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(3) the notice is as section 386AG(3)(a) and (b) require` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(3) the notice is as section 386AG(3)(a) and (b) require` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5): offences
#ASSERT `s 386AH(5) the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(5) the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(5) the officer of the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(5) the officer of the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(5) the most the company or foreign company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 386AH(5) the most the company or foreign company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6): the addressee: arguments: complied; the day complied; the date specified; the date asked
#ASSERT `s 386AH(6) the addressee has complied with the notice within the time specified` TRUE (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(6) the addressee has complied with the notice within the time specified` TRUE (Date 11 6 2026) (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(6) the addressee has complied with the notice within the time specified` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 10 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 386AH(6) the addressee is guilty of the offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(6) the addressee is guilty of the offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 386AH(6) the most the addressee may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 386AH(6) the most the addressee may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

